        {
          "type": "output_text",
          "text": "I confirmed the relevant work order is **MO-25-09-1070** (**WO-2025-09-004**, Cooler Plate Pack) at Modine’s Racine site. Its September cost period entered **Pending Close at 2025-09-30T18:00:00**.\n\nI could not verify whether a matching cost event was created after that time or establish its source transaction ID, amount, exact creation time, or recorded accounting status. The supporting-record source returned **403 — source role not granted**. Accordingly, I cannot calculate lateness or determine whether the recorded status is consistent with Oracle’s treatment. I have not inferred those values.\n\nThe accessible Oracle 26B policy excerpt says newly created transactions related to a period in Pending Close are not staged for accounting, and transactions created after the pending-close date are not processed until the period is closed or reopened. That policy alone does not establish what happened to this work order’s event.\n\nI kept the review read-only and did not modify business records. I submitted the available findings; the report receipt is **“needs_evidence.”** The audit artifact is saved at `/cache/work/worker_c16da747e169/audit-report.json`.",
